  "summary": "Traditional textile garments of the gaucho, including the poncho and chiripa, featuring distinctive patterns and craftsmanship.",
  "description": "Characterized by thick woolen ponchos with striped or geometric patterns and the chiripa (a short poncho or jacket), often with fringes and earthy color palettes. Developed by gauchos for practical protection from the elements while working in the Pampas, these garments evolved to include regional variations and symbolic patterns reflecting gaucho identity.",
  "culturalContext": "The historical \"gaucho\" is elusive, because there has been more than one kind.  Mythologisation has obscured the topic.",
